--- body ---
## Context
Design note: `conception/2026-10-31-skill-case-notes.md` (author's idea, 2026-10-31,
KISS-reviewed). Child of 1346: the census there shows Claude Code main sessions
almost never pull repository memory, so this pilot pushes it. Each project keeps
`memory/skills/<skill>.md`, four dated cases (latest, usual, best, worst) in the
case-method shape: context, what happened, reaction, outcome.

## Scope
Staged per the note § 4; each stage starts only when the previous read-back passes.
1. Claude Code: one script in `scripts/` via `idh-hook`, `PostToolUse` on `Skill`,
   marker-file dedup per session and agent, every outcome logged; the harness note
   `memory/skills/merge.md`.
2. Read-back on Claude: planted token quoted by the model; once per context; in a
   subagent; with a typed `/merge`.
3. Codex probe with a `SessionStart` positive control; wire Codex or fall back to step 0.
4. Pi wiring and read-back.

Not in scope: outcome measurement (1354 may add an arm), automatic note writing by
roar or smelt.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `memory/skills/merge.md` holds four dated, sourced cases; author has read it
- [ ] Claude read-back passes: token quoted, delivered once, also in a subagent and with a typed /merge
- [ ] Codex probe result recorded on this ticket, with its positive control
- [ ] Pi read-back passes, or the reason it was stopped is recorded
- [ ] The scoped gate passes

## Imagine (raid 3d5ae7)
- Premise holds: nothing merged on 2026-10-31 touches hooks or `memory/skills/` (absent). Hook source is `adapters/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json`, launcher `adapters/claude-code/bin/idh-hook`.
- Verified by headless probe (claude 2.1.316, haiku): PostToolUse matcher `Skill` payload carries `tool_input.skill`, `session_id`, `cwd`, and `agent_id` only inside a subagent; `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` reached the model (planted token quoted, main and subagent). A typed `/probe` as headless prompt also fired the hook; interactive TUI not verified.
- Antipatterns to avoid: unsanitised skill name (`^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*$`, strip `plugin:`), fail-closed on bad input (fail open, log), generalising for Codex/Pi before stage 3.

## Plan (raid 3d5ae7) — one PR, refs 1394, does not close it
- `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` (mode 755): payload → name → `git -C $cwd rev-parse --show-toplevel` → `memory/skills/<name>.md` → marker `${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/idh/skill-notes/<session>-<agent|main>` → JSON additionalContext under a declarative header, ~400-word cap. Log one line per outcome (delivered, no-note, already-delivered, no-skill-name, bad-name, parse-error).
- `adapters/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json`: PostToolUse matcher `Skill` via `idh-hook skill-case-notes.sh`, timeout 5.
- `memory/skills/merge.md`: four dated, sourced cases from the journal; no invented case.
- `tests/test_skill_case_notes.py`, first failing test `test_delivers_note_as_additional_context`; then dedup, agent_id re-delivery, no-note, bad name, plugin prefix, garbage stdin, subdirectory cwd, hooks.json wiring.
- Headless read-back (main, subagent, typed `/merge`) with log lines recorded on this ticket.
- Stages 3 (Codex) and 4 (Pi) become child tickets once stage 2 passes.

## Blind spot (raid 3d5ae7)
- Marker outlives compaction and `--resume` (same session_id): the note is not re-delivered after compaction. Accepted for the pilot, as § 3.4 defers it; the PR states the limit.
- Hook is user-scope and fires in every project: only plaintext `memory/skills/*.md` is read (encrypted files skipped and logged as no-note); notes are written by hand in the pilot; smelt does not write `memory/skills/`.
- The 1346 census counts tool reads of `memory/`; injected notes never appear there. The pilot is measured by the hook log.

## Feasibility (raid 3d5ae7)
- PASS. `tests/test_claude_code_adapter.py` checks the event set with `<=` and that every launched script exists; `idh-hook` requires the executable bit. No validator mirrors Claude hooks to Codex/Pi; no test sweeps `memory/` wholesale. Open PR #2049 touches `memory/topics/` and memory tests only, disjoint.

## Fix round: UserPromptSubmit trigger (raid 3d5ae7)
- Condition of design note § 3.5 met: a typed `/merge` never fired PostToolUse on Skill. `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` now also serves UserPromptSubmit, same marker as the Skill-tool path (typed then Skill tool, or the reverse, delivers once). Non-slash prompts exit in bash before python or git and log nothing.
- Payload probe (claude 2.1.316, haiku): UserPromptSubmit carries `session_id`, `cwd`, `hook_event_name`, `prompt` (raw, `/merge ...`), no `tool_input`; `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` with `hookEventName: UserPromptSubmit` reached the model.
- Read-back (headless, haiku, temp repo, planted token, `--allowedTools Skill`, real script wired on both events): prompt `/merge ...` answered with `PLANTED-TOKEN-RB-4410`; log: `delivered skill=merge session=35561396-0b00-4a8f-934f-def8ec806586 agent=main`, one line, one marker. A non-slash prompt (`hello`) created no log and no marker.
- Limit: read-back was `-p` mode; interactive TUI typing is the same hook path but not separately verified.
